+where $W_s$ is the causal state writer, $R_s$ is a bounded readout, $P$ is a
+fixed serializer, and $D_{M_m}$ is greedy decoding by the frozen reader. The
+foundation arm is exactly $s=0$, for which $E_{0,Q}=\varnothing$. For
+$s<s'$, a deterministic projection $\pi_{s'\rightarrow s}$ satisfies
+$Z_s=\pi_{s'\rightarrow s}(Z_{s'})$, so every larger budget is a strict
+refinement rather than a different representation.
+
+Each endpoint executes the same five operations: (i) write state from $X$
+before $Q$ and $Y$ are revealed; (ii) validate types, ordering, and the budget;
+(iii) select at most $s$ query-relevant entries; (iv) serialize those entries
+with the fixed canonical template; and (v) decode with the unchanged model and
+scorer. A failed validity check sets $E_{s,Q}=\varnothing$ and therefore
+returns the foundation path. Equation~\eqref{eq:ascent-contract} isolates the
+two experimental coordinates: $m$ changes only the frozen decoder, whereas
+$s$ changes only a nested external-state refinement. This is the executable
+counterpart of the information comparison in
